@startuml ResourceQueue
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
' purpose: resource admission and durable ownership of queued agent attempts
' covers: cmd/proveo/schedule.go
' covers: internal/schedule/schedule.go
' covers: internal/schedule/runner.go
' covers: internal/sbx/limits.go
' covers: internal/sbx/host_memory.go
' covers: internal/sbx/host_disk_unix.go
' covers: internal/sbx/host_disk_other.go
' covers: _spec/_experiments/dashboard/index.html
' covers: _spec/_experiments/dashboard/resource_queue.qnt
' status: EXPERIMENT. HTML runs a sample machine. The Go scheduler still
' launches calendar-due jobs directly. The host sampler and lease ledger
' are proposed runtime work.
' Related capacity model: _spec/_paradigms/resource_management.puml
' Workspace and graph: _spec/_experiments/dashboard/workspace-instances.puml
'
' HOST CAPACITY
' Sample on the sbx host. CPU topology and current guest CPU limits in
' internal/sbx/limits.go give a ceiling. Admission also needs host CPU
' utilization over an interval, expressed as integer millicores.
' Reuse Linux MemAvailable and macOS vm_stat parsing from host_memory.go
' for system RAM. The local-inference pool can be discrete VRAM.
' Reuse the Unix Statfs free-space helper for the actual sbx storage and
' retained-artifact filesystems. Deduplicate paths on one filesystem.
' Windows needs supported host probes. Totals and model-inference
' headroom alone are insufficient to label a sample current.
' Reserve operator headroom. Subtract every outstanding Proveo lease
' from the configured pool. Separately subtract unreflected reservations
' from the measured available resources. Admit against the componentwise
' minimum. Confirm each reservation was reflected before excluding it
' from that second subtraction. Track disk per filesystem in Go.
' Missing, stale, or unreconciled inputs pause new admissions while
' existing jobs continue. A resource change triggers a new evaluation.
'
' ADMISSION AND LIVENESS
' Serialize compare-and-reserve across Proveo queues on the same host.
' Record a durable lease before launching a job. Reconcile known VMs
' and job identities on restart. Hold leases through startup, execution,
' and result carry. An unreachable client retains its lease until
' inventory confirms the actual VM outcome.
' Release startup reservations on a verified no-start. Release runnable
' CPU and RAM after the VM is gone or stopped. Charge disk that remains
' to a fresh filesystem sample before admitting further writes. Refresh
' the sample when a reflected lease ends.
' Consider ready jobs in insertion order and take the oldest whose whole
' resource vector fits. Later small jobs can bypass an older large one.
' Continuous small jobs can starve a large one. Expose wait reasons and
' age. Decide a bounded bypass policy separately if contention warrants it.
' Queue items become ready through submission and prerequisite completion.
' A calendar hook can enqueue an item. It never bypasses admission.
' Runtime time limits and probe freshness still use clocks.
' Temporary resource pressure and unmet prerequisites keep a task queued.
' Invalid dependency graphs or unsatisfiable requests require attention.
' Keep workflow phase separate from admission state.
'
' QUINT EVALUATION
' resource_queue.qnt models two jobs, three integer resources, a sampled
' headroom, and which leases the sample reflects. Use Quint in verification
' to check that legal transitions respect the policy pool, keep reflected
' leases attached to held work, and honor prerequisites before admission.
' The model's scenarios cover each pressure dimension, unavailable samples,
' pending reservations, carry and resample, and a delayed prerequisite.
' Seven Quint scenarios passed. Apalache found no invariant violation
' within 12 transitions of this two-job model.
' Keep the live scheduler in Go. The model abstracts OS readings, fsync,
' lifecycle discovery and simultaneous processes. Cover those boundaries
' with Go adapter tests and live sbx verification when the runtime is built.
' Command: npx --yes @informalsystems/quint@0.34.0 test resource_queue.qnt
' Source: https://quint.sh/docs/getting-started

title Resource-driven task admission

state "Queued\nwait for prerequisites or resources" as Queued
state "Reserved\nhold CPU, RAM and disk before launch" as Reserved
state "Running\nhold through execution" as Running
state "Settling\nhold through outcome and Git carry" as Settling
state "Require attention\nreview, failure or invalid request" as Attention
state "Complete\naccepted work" as Complete

[*] --> Queued : submit
Queued --> Reserved : prerequisites cleared and vector fits
Queued --> Attention : invalid graph or request
Reserved --> Running : VM and agent started
Reserved --> Attention : launch failed and no VM holds lease
Running --> Settling : agent stopped or outcome recovered
Settling --> Attention : results published or operator input needed
Attention --> Queued : operator requeues
Attention --> Complete : work accepted
Complete --> [*]
@enduml
